- **Hook Organization**
  - Place hooks in the appropriate directory based on their scope:
  ```
  frontend/src/hooks/        # Application-wide, general-purpose hooks
  ├── useConfig.ts          # Global configuration and styles
  └── other global hooks...
  
  frontend/src/lib/hooks/   # Feature-specific, specialized hooks
  ├── use-payment-flow.ts   # Payment feature logic
  ├── use-user-profile.ts   # User profile management
  ├── use-file-upload.ts    # File upload handling
  └── other feature hooks...
  ```

  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Import from correct location based on hook type
  // Global hooks
  import { useConfig } from '@/hooks/useConfig';
  
  // Feature-specific hooks
  import { usePaymentFlow } from '@/lib/hooks/use-payment-flow';
  ```

  - **Global Hooks** (`@/hooks/`)
    - Used across multiple features
    - Handle application-wide concerns
    - Provide shared functionality
    - Example: Configuration, theming, authentication

  - **Feature Hooks** (`@/lib/hooks/`)
    - Specific to a single feature
    - Encapsulate complex feature logic
    - Handle specific workflows
    - Example: Payment flow, user profile, file upload
    
